<title>USA: Clinton authorizes disaster relief for Tennessee.</title>
<headline>Clinton authorizes disaster relief for Tennessee.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton Wednesday designed five Tennessee countries as disaster areas because of severe storms and tornadoes that battered the state March 28.</p>
<p>Clinton's action makes victims of storm damage in Bradley, Hamilton, Polk, Sequatchie and Smith counties eligible for federal disaster relief, including grants and low interest loans to finance repairs.</p>
</text>
